# =============================================================================
# ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION TEMPLATE
# =============================================================================
# This file serves as a template for required environment variables.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual values.
#
# SECURITY NOTES:
# - NEVER commit the actual .env file to version control
# - Rotate keys immediately if they are exposed
# - Use different keys for development, staging, and production
# - The .env file is already in .gitignore
# - Store production secrets in your deployment platform's secret manager
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLIENT-SIDE ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (Vite - Exposed to Browser)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These variables are prefixed with VITE_ and are embedded in the client bundle.
# DO NOT put sensitive secrets here - only public/publishable keys.

# Supabase Configuration (Client)
# Get these from: Supabase Dashboard > Project Settings > API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-anon-key-here
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id

# Stripe Configuration (Client)
# Get this from: Stripe Dashboard > Developers > API Keys
# This is the PUBLISHABLE key (safe to expose in browser)
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_your-stripe-publishable-key

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-SIDE ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (Supabase Edge Functions)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These variables are used by Supabase Edge Functions and should be configured
# in your Supabase project settings under Edge Functions > Environment Variables.
# They are NOT exposed to the client.

# Supabase Configuration (Server)
# Get these from: Supabase Dashboard > Project Settings > API
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key-here

# Stripe Configuration
# Get these from: Stripe Dashboard > Developers > API Keys
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_your-stripe-secret-key
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_your-webhook-secret

# Resend Email Configuration
# Get this from: Resend Dashboard > API Keys
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_your-resend-api-key

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEPLOYMENT INSTRUCTIONS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# For Local Development:
# 1. Copy this file to .env
# 2. Fill in the VITE_* variables with your development Supabase credentials
# 3. Server-side variables are configured in Supabase Dashboard for Edge Functions
#
# For Production:
# 1. Configure VITE_* variables in your hosting platform (Vercel, Netlify, etc.)
# 2. Configure server-side variables in Supabase Dashboard:
#    - Go to Edge Functions > Environment Variables
#    - Add STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET, RESEND_API_KEY
#    - SUPABASE_* variables are automatically available in Edge Functions
#
# For CI/CD:
# 1. Store all secrets in your CI/CD platform's secret manager
# 2. Never log or expose secret values in build outputs
# 3. Use different secrets for each environment (dev, staging, prod)
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED VARIABLES BY ENVIRONMENT
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Client (Browser):
#   - VITE_SUPABASE_URL (required)
#   - VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY (required)
#   - VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID (required)
#   - VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY (required for payment features)
#
# Server (Edge Functions):
#   - SUPABASE_URL (auto-provided by Supabase)
#   - SUPABASE_ANON_KEY (auto-provided by Supabase)
#   - SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (auto-provided by Supabase)
#   - STRIPE_SECRET_KEY (required for payment functions)
#   - STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET (required for webhook verification)
#   - RESEND_API_KEY (required for email functions)
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
